SYNTHETIC run directories — not real benchmark rows
These commands were captured from the real summarize module.

### clean synthetic run: scores, failure kinds, agreement
$ uv run --frozen python -m parallel_search_evals.summarize run_dir=/tmp/pse-demo/clean-synthetic
suite: hle
search_engine: baseline
model: gpt-fixture
provider: openai
source_sha256: aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
records found: 3
completed: 2
failed: 1
correct: 1
score: 0.3333333333333333
failure kinds:
  TimeoutError: 1
saved summary: agrees
exit: 0

### write CSV from the clean synthetic run
$ uv run --frozen python -m parallel_search_evals.summarize run_dir=/tmp/pse-demo/clean-synthetic csv=/tmp/pse-demo/clean-synthetic.csv
suite: hle
search_engine: baseline
model: gpt-fixture
provider: openai
source_sha256: aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
records found: 3
completed: 2
failed: 1
correct: 1
score: 0.3333333333333333
failure kinds:
  TimeoutError: 1
saved summary: agrees
exit: 0

### show CSV contents
$ cat /tmp/pse-demo/clean-synthetic.csv
task_id,status,correct,score,failure_kind
task-a,completed,true,1.0,
task-b,completed,false,0.0,
task-c,failed,false,0.0,TimeoutError
exit: 0

### show CSV permissions
$ ls -l /tmp/pse-demo/clean-synthetic.csv
-rw------- 1 ubuntu ubuntu 134 Nov 18 01:51 /tmp/pse-demo/clean-synthetic.csv
exit: 0

